arm64: dts: rockchip: khadas-edge: USB PD sink on both USB-C ports (FUSB302)

Khadas Edge1, Android 14 on mainline 6.12. Applied to kernel/mainline by
build/build-kernel.sh before every build (device/khadas/edge/kernel/patches/).

The Edge module takes its power through either USB-C port into a BQ25703
charger (5-20V in), and each port has a FUSB302 that negotiates the voltage
with the supply over USB PD - in software. Khadas' own 4.4 kernel does that
(fusb0 on i2c8, fusb1 on i2c4, both at 0x22, interrupts GPIO1_A2 and GPIO4_D6,
asking for up to 13V, i.e. 12V); mainline describes neither chip, so nothing
asks and a PD supply stays at 5V. Card 24 reset five times in a row, with
nothing in ramoops - no panic, no oops - each within a minute or two of
Android starting, when every core and the GPU are busy: a brownout.

Both FUSB302s are described here for the mainline fusb302/tcpm drivers, as
sinks asking for 5, 9 or 12V at up to 3A (tcpm takes the highest power the
supply offers among them). VBUS is never sourced on these ports, so the
port-0 VBUS switch (GPIO4_D2 in Khadas' tree) is not touched and the vbus
supply is a placeholder regulator. tcpm in 6.12 does not hard-reset a supply
that was already providing VBUS when it probed: Soft_Reset first, then
Get_Source_Cap - a hard reset would cut the board's own power.

The boot script can rewrite sink-pdos or disable both nodes before booting
(pd= in edge1-options.txt), so a supply that misbehaves needs no rebuild.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
index c772985ae..87da6d5f2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge.dtsi
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/input/linux-event-codes.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pwm/pwm.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/usb/pd.h>
 #include "rk3399.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -834,3 +835,81 @@ &vopl {
 &vopl_mmu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * USB-C power: both ports feed the board's charger (a BQ25703, 5-20V in) through
+ * a FUSB302 each, and the voltage is whatever the board asks the supply for over
+ * USB PD - nothing asks without these nodes, so a PD supply stays at 5V and the
+ * board browns out under load. Khadas' own kernel asks for 12V. Sink only: the
+ * board never sources VBUS on these ports here, so their VBUS switch (GPIO4_D2
+ * on port 0) is left alone and the supply is a placeholder.
+ *
+ * The sink PDOs are 5, 9 and 12V; the boot script can replace them or disable
+ * the controllers (pd= in edge1-options.txt).
+ */
+/ {
+	vbus_typec_sink: vbus-typec-sink {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vbus_typec_sink";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c4 {
+	fusb1: usb-typec@22 {
+		compatible = "fcs,fusb302";
+		reg = <0x22>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio4>;
+		interrupts = <RK_PD6 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&fusb1_int>;
+		vbus-supply = <&vbus_typec_sink>;
+
+		connector {
+			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
+			label = "USB-C 1";
+			data-role = "dual";
+			power-role = "sink";
+			op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
+			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
+				     PDO_FIXED(9000, 3000, 0)
+				     PDO_FIXED(12000, 3000, 0)>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c8 {
+	fusb0: usb-typec@22 {
+		compatible = "fcs,fusb302";
+		reg = <0x22>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio1>;
+		interrupts = <RK_PA2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&fusb0_int>;
+		vbus-supply = <&vbus_typec_sink>;
+
+		connector {
+			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
+			label = "USB-C 0";
+			data-role = "dual";
+			power-role = "sink";
+			op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
+			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
+				     PDO_FIXED(9000, 3000, 0)
+				     PDO_FIXED(12000, 3000, 0)>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&pinctrl {
+	usb-typec {
+		fusb0_int: fusb0-int {
+			rockchip,pins = <1 RK_PA2 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_up>;
+		};
+
+		fusb1_int: fusb1-int {
+			rockchip,pins = <4 RK_PD6 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_up>;
+		};
+	};
+};
